From ef1719208a431258f48915768144be85183a0c6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iuri Jikidze <37273763+ijiki16@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:14:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/39] net: stmmac: dwmac-sun60i: program syscfg out of reset,
 enable PHY clock

Fix two differences from the vendor glue. They were found while the
external RGMII PHY on the OrangePi 4 Pro was unreachable ("mdio_bus
stmmac-0: MDIO device at address 1 is missing"):

1. sun60i_gmac_syscfg() wrote the glue register while the GMAC bus
   clock was gated and its bus reset asserted. The write is dropped and
   the register stays at its reset value 0x8000 (PHY_SEL = internal
   EPHY, no RGMII, no delays), so the MAC reports "GMII/MII" and MDIO
   never reaches the external PHY. Ungate the "stmmaceth" bus clock and
   deassert the (shared) "ahb" bus reset before writing it, as the
   vendor dwmac-sunxi does.

2. The 25 MHz PHY reference fanout (CCU GMAC0_PHY_CLK, routed to PH15
   "RGMII0-EPHY-25/50M") is listed as the "phy" clock but nothing enables
   it; it resets gated (0x1410 = 0x00000005). The vendor driver enables
   it when "aw,soc-phy-clk-en" is set, and the vendor OrangePi 4 Pro DT
   sets that. Enable it when present. Whether this board needs the clock
   is untested: its schematic also shows a crystal on the PHY.

With both, the glue register reads 0x00011145 (identical to the vendor
6.6 kernel), the MAC reports "Active PHY interface: RGMII (1)", and the
CCU shows GMAC0_PHY_CLK = 0x80000005.

Tested on an OrangePi 4 Pro (A733, YT8531C) on top of the
"match GMAC0 reset roles" dts change, together with the board-level
settings that also turned out to be required (MDC divider, PHY supply,
PHY reset GPIO, phy-handle, PHY CLK_OUT and RGMII delays, see the
OrangePi 4 Pro SD dts): link up, DHCP, ping and SSH work. Not tested on
any other A733 board or with gmac1.

This change was made with the help of an AI coding assistant (Claude);
the problem was found by comparing register dumps between the vendor
and mainline kernels on the board.

Fixes: b14cbb33a230 ("net: stmmac: add Allwinner A733 GMAC-210 glue")
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun60i.c    | 37 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun60i.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun60i.c
index b8846ae6e..5bb7d0e5d 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun60i.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-sun60i.c
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
 #include <linux/phy.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/regulator/consumer.h>
+#include <linux/reset.h>
 #include <linux/stmmac.h>
 
 #include "stmmac.h"
@@ -101,6 +102,7 @@ static int sun60i_gmac_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	struct plat_stmmacenet_data *plat_dat;
 	struct stmmac_resources stmmac_res;
 	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
+	struct reset_control *rst;
 	struct clk *clk;
 	void __iomem *syscfg_base;
 	int ret;
@@ -122,15 +124,42 @@ static int sun60i_gmac_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	plat_dat->flags |= STMMAC_FLAG_SPH_DISABLE;
 	plat_dat->host_dma_width = 32;
 
-	ret = sun60i_gmac_syscfg(dev, syscfg_base, plat_dat);
-	if (ret)
-		return ret;
-
 	clk = devm_clk_get_enabled(dev, "mbus");
 	if (IS_ERR(clk))
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(clk),
 				     "Failed to get or enable MBUS clock\n");
 
+	/*
+	 * The glue (syscfg) block sits behind the GMAC bus clock and bus reset.
+	 * Written while that reset is still asserted, the write is dropped and
+	 * the register keeps its reset value 0x8000 (PHY_SEL = internal EPHY),
+	 * so MDIO never reaches the external PHY. Release the bus reset (shared
+	 * with stmmac's "ahb" reset) and ungate the bus clock first, as the
+	 * vendor dwmac-sunxi does.
+	 */
+	clk = devm_clk_get_enabled(dev, "stmmaceth");
+	if (IS_ERR(clk))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(clk),
+				     "Failed to get or enable GMAC bus clock\n");
+
+	rst = devm_reset_control_get_optional_shared_deasserted(dev, "ahb");
+	if (IS_ERR(rst))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(rst),
+				     "Failed to deassert GMAC bus reset\n");
+
+	/*
+	 * 25 MHz PHY reference fanout (PH15). It is gated at reset and nothing
+	 * else enables it. The vendor DT enables it with "aw,soc-phy-clk-en".
+	 */
+	clk = devm_clk_get_optional_enabled(dev, "phy");
+	if (IS_ERR(clk))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(clk),
+				     "Failed to get or enable PHY clock\n");
+
+	ret = sun60i_gmac_syscfg(dev, syscfg_base, plat_dat);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	ret = devm_regulator_get_enable_optional(dev, "phy");
 	if (ret)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "Failed to get or enable PHY supply\n");
